      "title": "CVE-2026-4603",
      "summary": "Versions of the package jsrsasign before 11.1.1 are vulnerable to Division by zero due to the RSASetPublic/KEYUTIL parsing path in ext/rsa.js and the BigInteger.modPowInt reduction logic in ext/jsbn.js. An attacker can force RSA public-key operations (e.g., verify and encryption) to collapse to deterministic zero outputs and hide “invalid key” errors by supplying a JWK whose modulus decodes to zero.",
      "raw_text": null,
      "published_at": "2026-03-23T06:16:22.233000Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-04-02T13:31:49.388525Z",
